1
00:00:03,904 --> 00:00:05,074
(Leonard:)The math is all there.

2
00:00:05,239 --> 00:00:07,149
(Leonard:)-It's not real.
-Yes, it is.

3
00:00:07,307 --> 00:00:10,377
(Sheldon:)Look.
It is scientifically impossible

4
00:00:10,544 --> 00:00:12,424
(Sheldon:)for a person to tip a cow.

5
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:15,194
(Sheldon:)Even you, with your stocky build

6
00:00:15,349 --> 00:00:17,019
(Sheldon:)and lumberjack shoulders,
you couldn't do it.

7
00:00:18,719 --> 00:00:21,029
(Raj:)It's horrible. Why would you push
a cow over? They're sacred.

8
00:00:21,188 --> 00:00:22,258
(Penny:)Oh, stop it.

9
00:00:22,422 --> 00:00:24,262
(Penny:)I've seen you eat,
like, a million hamburgers.

10
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:27,094
(Raj:)Hey, an animal can be both
sacred and delicious.

11
00:00:28,262 --> 00:00:30,042
Lock, I'm telling you
I've done it, okay?

12
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:31,767
(Penny:)I clearly remember
the cow standing up

13
00:00:31,932 --> 00:00:33,272
(Penny:)and then the cow on its side.

14
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:35,243
(Leonard:)Were you drunk?

15
00:00:35,402 --> 00:00:38,782
(Penny:)I was 16 in Nebraska.
What do you think?

16
00:00:38,939 --> 00:00:41,719
(Leonard:)I think you're the one who fell over.

17
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:45,785
(Penny:)That would explain why the sky
was also on its side.

18
00:00:46,513 --> 00:00:48,423
(Raj:)-Hey.
-Howard.

19
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:49,962
(Penny:)real or not?

20
00:00:50,117 --> 00:00:52,357
I'm going to say... not.

21
00:00:52,519 --> 00:00:54,429
(Howard:)That's just based on me
trying to roll

22
00:00:54,588 --> 00:00:56,728
(Howard:)my mom over
when she's snoring.

23
00:00:57,925 --> 00:01:00,805
(Howard:)Speaking of that big side of beef,

24
00:01:00,961 --> 00:01:04,271
(Howard:)she's invited all of you
to Thanksgiving at her house.

25
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:05,941
(Howard:)Mmm.

26
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:08,977
(Sheldon:)You know, I've been told
that a bald refusal

27
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:11,306
(Sheldon:)of an invitation is rude
and one must instead

28
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:13,141
(Sheldon:)offer up a polite excuse, so...

29
00:01:13,307 --> 00:01:15,617
(Sheldon:)I'd love to go, but, unfortunately,

30
00:01:15,776 --> 00:01:17,656
(Sheldon:)that sounds awful.

31
00:01:21,148 --> 00:01:22,958
(Howard:)Come on, it'll be fun.

32
00:01:23,116 --> 00:01:24,286
(Penny:)We were actually
going to do it here.

33
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:26,051
(Howard:)Please?
Bernadette's bringing her dad,

34
00:01:26,219 --> 00:01:27,159
because her mom's out of town,

35
00:01:27,321 --> 00:01:29,301
(Howard:)and I never have anything
to say to that guy.

36
00:01:29,456 --> 00:01:31,666
(Sheldon:)Since you put it that way,
I'd love to go,

37
00:01:31,825 --> 00:01:33,565
(Sheldon:)but that sounds even more awful.

38
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:35,901
(Leonard:)It'd actually be nice to not hear

39
00:01:36,063 --> 00:01:37,663
(Leonard:)Sheldon complain
about my cooking all day.

40
00:01:37,831 --> 00:01:39,071
(Sheldon:)Excuse me,

41
00:01:39,232 --> 00:01:41,942
(Sheldon:)but every year
you prepare a terrible meal

42
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:44,082
(Sheldon:)and every year I criticize it.

43
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:46,577
(Sheldon:)Do our traditions
mean nothing to you?

44
00:01:48,742 --> 00:01:50,152
(Leonard:)-I want to go.
-Yeah, me, too.

45
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:51,520
(Raj:)-I'm in.
-Sheldon.

46
00:01:51,678 --> 00:01:53,988
(Sheldon:)Fine, I'll go.

47
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:56,427
(Sheldon:)But if her food is delicious,
Thanksgiving is ruined,

48
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:57,753
(Sheldon:)and it's on you.

49
00:01:59,686 --> 00:02:01,826
I (THEME SONG PLAYS) I

